<section id="questions" class="section-wrap faq-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">A FEW THINGS YOU MIGHT WONDER</p><h2>Good questions.</h2><p>A clear picture before you get started.</p></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Is LifeOS a task manager or a habit tracker?</summary><p>Both, connected to your life goals. Boards organize your tasks and projects. Your timetable makes room for routines, your habit tracker records check-ins, and Overview and Insights help you see patterns across them.</p></details><details><summary>Can I start using it immediately?</summary><p>Access is currently set up manually. Submit the form and we’ll contact you about availability and next steps. An access request is not an automatic account creation.</p></details><details><summary>How much does it cost?</summary><p>Pricing is not published yet. We’ll explain any costs before setting up your account. Requesting access doesn’t require a payment card or commit you to a subscription.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use it with friends or family?</summary><p>Yes. Share a board using invitation links and choose viewer, reviewer, or editor access. Personal routines and habit history aren’t automatically shared with board members.</p></details><details><summary>Does it track my actual working time?</summary><p>LifeOS calculates scheduled hours and completed-time estimates from timed tasks and checked habits. It does not currently run a stopwatch or record actual elapsed working time.</p></details><details><summary>Will it work on my phone?</summary><p>LifeOS runs in your web browser with layouts for phones, tablets, and desktops. You don’t need to install a native mobile app.</p></details></div></section>
